A||N||5||Boxdin||My Formula beat RX-7 and TR6 among others in club race||||6||
Z||000000||Boxdin||05-16-2000||12:14 PM||||This weekend was the first race weekend on new 1,7 mile road course track in Albuquerque, and my 5 sp Formula with 133k miles smoked lots of other cars. Great fun too!! I'm thinking of trying my Formula      A/T next time, it might actually be faster than 5 sp due to tightness of corners and my having a tough time in very hard right corners doing clutch and left hand only steering while sliding hard left in seat. (did that make sense ?) The pedal offset to the right made those turns very difficult.  ||||reg||6
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||05-16-2000||03:00 PM||||Congratulations, you did your Fiero proud!||||reg||14
Z||000002||lowCG||05-17-2000||12:44 AM||||Sounds like lots of fun,maybe you need to modify a seat to fit you better,and bolt it in for the races.<BR>Mine gave me a sore butt after a couple days when traveling,might try to expiriment with some foam on my car.My friend had his Lancia Monte Carlo seats redone,and had some foam removed from the seat with great success;you now sit in the seat,instead of on it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||frontal lobe||05-17-2000||01:01 AM||||Way to go!  Sounds like fun.  Any close encounters with other cars?  Wouldn't want to hurt the Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-17-2000||09:42 AM||||Congrats!  Which gen RX7??  The TR6s weren't meant for speed.  Neither were the 7s or 8s, but they were vastly improved.  Are you sure it wasn't a TR7 or TR8 you wasted?  Those were the ones that looked sort of like a Fiero coupe.  The TR6s looked like an MGB on steroids.  Seriously cool cars, but not really racing material in todays world.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Boxdin||05-17-2000||02:13 PM||||Lots of close encounters, but none unplanned, and no touching ( touching in our club is an automatic 13 month suspension of licence). The RX-7 was a 12A, not a 13B, but he had racing tires ( I had street tires).  And the Triumph was for sure a TR-6. A ton of fun was had by all. Two people rented Geo Metros for the weekend and raced them on the track too. Don't know what they said when they broughht the cars back with very worn tires. Lots of Bugeyes, two road race Cougars( 67&68 ) some Porsches, and some other british stuff were present. All in all, a great club event with quality people. My Fiero initially got some funny looks, but after the first run, people started saying how neat Fieros are !!||||reg||6
